	(text "C1 30 W: 9 V, 5 V branches (planned, the user's 2026-10-15 layout)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 92.71 77.47 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
				(bold yes)
				(italic yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2276982e-015c-4a82-b8c8-d61ca506378f")
	)
	(text "C2 22.5 W: the Pi 4 at 5 V 3 A (sheet Host).\nNever from a 12 V -> 5 V buck."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 66.04 170.18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "50d0261b-3ae1-4c27-9e63-03642684af54")
	)
	(text "POWER: one USB-C PD charger, three branches"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "602ec99a-8436-4526-a2cf-dd16d88169f1")
	)
	(text "+9V feeds the two MP1495s:\n- MP_Buck0 on the Aux PCB (sheet Aux MCU): +5V_LED, the Aux MCU,\n  the LEDs, the buzzer.\n- MP_Buck1 on the hub board (sheet Hub board): +5V_TOOL_IN, the\n  tool (switched by U1006 + F1001) the bed and +5V_SW (U956, U957 on the plot bed board)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 167.64 93.98 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "684acd5b-6200-498c-a8a9-1c24df358c12")
	)
	(text "NOTES"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 200.66 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6f4f7da3-ef83-49f2-a634-62f3cdd2c26c")
	)
	(text "+7V5_ZK: the Melzi's Z and K drivers (their 12 V trace cut).\nSet 7.2-7.5 V today. The A4982 wants VBB >= 8 V:\n9 V for margin (motor heat is Vref, not the supply)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 236.22 40.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "822b1e4c-958d-46ac-bc2d-a4486137e36b")
	)
	(text "C0 45 W: 12 V, motion"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 92.71 26.67 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8cf3018b-fd87-46bf-9cc1-cde0b8bbb9d3")
	)
	(text "- Grounds: one ground point near the Melzi, one solid GND wire between the 9 V and 12 V branches there, so stepper\n  return never uses USB cables or signal wires. All GND on these sheets is that one net.\n- No backfeed: ~1 k in series on every line crossing supplies; USB VBUS of the Pi never tied to a buck's 5 V.\n- A fuse or e-fuse per branch (to do): a short anywhere trips the whole charger, every port off.\n- The charger cuts all its ports when a device is plugged into another: careful with hot-plugging.\n- 47-100 uF electrolytic at each MP1495's input (hot-plug ringing ~2 x Vin).\n- From docs/block-diagrams.md (the user's layout) and limn/TODO.md, Toolhead and harness rework."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 205.74 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "aa8c745d-68f8-4b00-b0f5-7e1f66521c91")
	)
	(text "+12V (switched): the Melzi's VIN and the LM2596 (sheet Melzi).\nThe switch only cuts motion."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 162.56 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c37927a5-ee11-4654-9590-542b88844835")
	)
	(text "+12V also feeds the LM2596 (LM_Buck0) by the Melzi\n(sheet Melzi): +7V5_ZK, the motors only."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 210.82 50.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f9d607d8-b4b9-4d14-98c5-b93315b354e5")
	)
